            <ArticleTitle>Diversity and culture; threads in a golden tapestry which nurses have the privilege to enact and the responsibility to preserve.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocn.14187</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reflecting upon my nursing career over the last twenty-five years, comparing the person I was at the start and the person I am now; there is a vast difference. Prior to starting my nursing training I had little experience of the world; I integrated with and was influenced by individuals and my local community and whilst I heard about wider aspects of UK society and the world on television, I had little direct experience. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</AbstractText>
